CBraMod receives its input in units of 100 µV, the scale it was pretrained and fine-tuned on by its authors: the backend divides the microvolt input by 100, for embeddings and for fine-tuning. It was given plain microvolts, 100 times that scale. A model's scale is `input_scale` in its registry entry. A model that expects microvolts now raises an error on volt-scale input, when fitting, predicting and extracting embeddings; extraction only warned and fine-tuning did not check.
